"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2891460235","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106593#issuecomment-2891460235","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106593","id":2891460235,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sWC6L","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-19T15:31:57Z","updated_at":"2025-05-19T15:58:30Z","body":"I see this adds a new property that acts as a secondary sorting offset for objects whose depth is identical (which acts different to the existing one). Is there a proposal tracking it? This should be discussed in a proposal to make sure there's an established need for it.\r\n\r\n> I don't know why the docs check failed for Linux / Editor w/ Mono given that it is giving me a completely incorrect sorting_stacked_offset that isn't an int so I wonder if the system is confusing sorting_offset and sorting_stacked_offset so I don't know what the problem mainly because\r\n\r\nYou need to reorder the property in the generated class reference to follow alphabetical order. I suggest running `--doctool` locally and committing the result.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2891460235/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892634641","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106593#issuecomment-2892634641","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106593","id":2892634641,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6sahoR","user":{"login":"Faolan-Rad","id":46481567,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NDgxNTY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46481567?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad","html_url":"https://github.com/Faolan-Rad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-20T01:21:01Z","updated_at":"2025-05-20T01:21:01Z","body":"> I see this adds a new property that acts as a secondary sorting offset for objects whose depth is identical (which acts different to the existing one). Is there a proposal tracking it? This should be discussed in a proposal to make sure there's an established need for it.\r\n> \r\n> > I don't know why the docs check failed for Linux / Editor w/ Mono given that it is giving me a completely incorrect sorting_stacked_offset that isn't an int so I wonder if the system is confusing sorting_offset and sorting_stacked_offset so I don't know what the problem mainly because\r\n> \r\n> You need to reorder the property in the generated class reference to follow alphabetical order. I suggest running `--doctool` locally and committing the result.\r\n\r\nI realized the property methods where set to float by accident \r\nAlso I renamed stacked sorting offset to -> sorting stacked order \r\nto more easily imply what it does ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2892634641/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2896398563","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106593#issuecomment-2896398563","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106593","id":2896398563,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6so4jj","user":{"login":"Faolan-Rad","id":46481567,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NDgxNTY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46481567?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad","html_url":"https://github.com/Faolan-Rad","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faolan-Rad/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-21T02:44:48Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T02:44:48Z","body":"> Could you provide some details about why you added `sorting_stacked_order` \r\n\r\nSo in my use case I am implementing a 3D UI for VR [Talking about the problem](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/12214#issuecomment-2796790430) its also disgusting to use a float in order to control z ordering\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2896398563/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2896398726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106593#issuecomment-2896398726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106593","id":2896398726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6so4mG","user":{"login":"Lielay9","id":40064911,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwMDY0OTEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/40064911?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9","html_url":"https://github.com/Lielay9","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lielay9/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-21T02:44:56Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T02:44:56Z","body":"> Could you provide some details about why you added `sorting_stacked_order` it seems to solve the same issue that the existing sort_offset does. We discussed doing something similar to `sorting_stacked_order` but decided to go with the sort_offset instead, although I can't remember the exact reason.\r\n\r\nComing from the perspective of 2.5D game (flat entities rendered in transparent pass in 3D environment):\r\nThe `sort_offset` is quite unwieldy in many cases as adjusting it in one place has the chain reaction of effectively requiring changing it on every transparent mesh. There are many cases where'd you want something to be on the same depth plane but have control over the order. I for example layer entities in the following way: player characters on top of enemies, and elite enemies on top of basic enemies etc. To have this kind of layering with `sort_offset` all transparent meshes need to be manually sorted by depth so that the entities don't overlap the game environment or other entities closer to the camera. \r\n\r\nThe `sorting_stacked_order` here is far better suitable for this purpose as no sorting is needed, the entities can simply be organized based on their priority to their own `sorting_stacked_order` value. This is also makes dynamically sorting/layering the entities far easier, for example layering the entities based on their remaining health.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2896398726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2897168901","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106593#issuecomment-28971689